{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416019-larp-rules-on-tabletop","id":1416019,"title":"LARP Rules on Tabletop?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-29T12:29:38-07:00","id":1416019,"title":"LARP Rules on Tabletop?","content":"I have heard people talk about using the LARP rules (character creation, etc) for tabletop. The resolution changes to a d6?<br /> <br /> Foes anyone know where this conversion is? Or how would I go about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T14:56:34-07:00","id":1416031,"title":"","content":"There's probably not any 'conversion' written as, outside of things that require step measurement, you don't really NEED to convert anything. Convert steps to meters. Use a d6 for resolution if you have to use a die, or use RPS as normal. Use the rest of the book as written. Done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T09:03:55-07:00","id":1416276,"title":"","content":"That sounds eerily familiar. I have a homebrew rules set that is based on some MUSH rules that were developed from the original LARP rules. It's called Vampire: Degeneration. It uses a d6 for resolution of pretty much everything. You can read a little bit about it on this thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1255173-just-completed-vampire-degeneration-v-1-5\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...neration-v-1-5</a> <br /> <br /> This may possibly even be what you've heard people talking about, but I don't think my stuff is widespread enough for that to have happened.<br /> <br /> A link to the most current public release of the main rulebook is here: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/g6yuikeoa903u2e/Degeneration%201-5%20Final-op.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/g6yuikeoa9...al-op.pdf?dl=0</a><br /> <br /> There's a version 1.75 in the works that is almost done. Should be ready in about three months. I've gotten sidetracked working on my homebrew setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}